    <expertiseList>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockList":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/8350d0fc3f184eacaab4684fbddf5bbc"},{"contentUdi":"umb://element/e9154552f25741659402b9d069318070"},{"contentUdi":"umb://element/38eecaab348b42808f91f27a4c30f199"}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/8350d0fc3f184eacaab4684fbddf5bbc","PropType":null,"stringItemText":"Geotechnical Investigations"},{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/e9154552f25741659402b9d069318070","PropType":null,"stringItemText":"Concrete Testing and Investigations"},{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/38eecaab348b42808f91f27a4c30f199","PropType":null,"stringItemText":"Soil Testing and Investigations"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </expertiseList>
    <grid>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/35b9acd4275b41f787eb12fa8d2a5d50","areas":[],"columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"9a4f7c2e-1b3d-4e8a-bf01-7d62a8f5c930","udi":"umb://element/35b9acd4275b41f787eb12fa8d2a5d50","content":"\u003cdiv class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"758bl\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe rich ore deposits of the Northern Cape fuel some of the largest mining operations in South Africa, with vast quantities of manganese and iron ore extracted from mines like Mamatwan, Wessels, Khumani, and Sishen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStarting early in the morning, Roadlab vehicles cover great distances each day, ferrying samples of soil and other local materials from mines across the Northern Cape.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese long trips are nothing compared to the journey the minerals from these mines will undertake in the months to come. After being carefully processed, the ore embarks on a journey across the country to the port of Richards Bay, which connects the Northern Cape’s minerals to global markets.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom Richards Bay, South African manganese and iron travels across the world to be transformed into the lithium-ion batteries and steel in the world’s next generation of electric vehicles, bridges and skyscrapers.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/0zxamvrm/sishen-3.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ehttps://www.angloamericankumba.com/our-business/operations\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eMamatwan and Wessels Mine\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe’ve had the privilege of working alongside great partners at these sites over the past 15 months, supporting new large-scale infrastructure developments at Mamatwan and Wessels Mines.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur partners were tasked with constructing new railway lines to connect these manganese-rich sites to the existing transport network, along with building new internal roads and a dam.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow that the railway lines are fully operational, these mines will be able to transport manganese more efficiently while ensuring the new infrastructure will meet the demands of decades to come. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur team was there every step of the way, providing essential quality control services to ensure the integrity and longevity of these critical structures.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe conducted a variety of geotechnical and materials testing, including density tests, Dynamic Cone Penetrometer (DCP) tests and continuous sampling for concrete strength assessments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur work included creating concrete cubes for strength testing and sampling for material classifications and Unconfined Compressive Strength (UCS) tests during stabilization phases.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/izcduqhf/mamatwan-wessels.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/tp1cit0m/mamatwan-wessels-2.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/hvkja15m/mamatwan-wessels-3.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eKhumani Mine\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKhumani Mine has been another long-term project for us, where we’ve been involved in multiple phases of expansion and infrastructure development over the years.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne of South Africa’s largest iron-ore producers, Khumani mine- based some 30km for Kathu - has grown in capacity from 10 million tonnes of export-quality iron ore each year to 14 million tonnes a year.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs contractors have worked on new areas of the mine over the years, we have been there, providing vital quality control testing including material classification and comprehensive geotechnical investigations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur work at Khumani has included a ful scope on on-site and laboratory testing - density testing, Deep Cone Penetrometers and occasional coring, material classifications, concrete strength tests—to ensure each new structure is built to last.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKhumani may be constantly evolving, but we remain a steady partner, ensuring that all projects meet therequired quality standards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/h5ybn1li/khumani-mine.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eSishen Mine\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSishen Mine is one of the largest open-pit mining operations in the world and a major player in South Africa’s iron ore industry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, we’re engaged in several major projects, including the G80 Solar Project, a new dump, a jig and slime facility and the Lyleveld intersection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith new construction expected to continue at Sishen for the next 20 years, we’re excited to be a trusted partner in their ongoing growth and development. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSishen Mine has been a core site for Roadlab since we established our operations in Kathu. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom density tests and DCPs to concrete strength assessments, Schmidt hammer tests and plate bearing tests, we’re conducting a wide array of quality control procedures. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, we’re performing soil sampling for California Bearing Ratio (CBR), UCS, and foundation indicators, ensuring the materials meet the rigorous demands of the mine’s expanding operations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/5cpl2p12/sishen-1.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/ibslhyow/sishen-2.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/0zxamvrm/sishen-3.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr /\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eInterested in our work?\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eReach out to us.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </grid>
    <heroContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "markup": "<p>Roadlab is an accomplished supporter of South Africa’s largest mining operations,&nbsp;<br>over 400 construction companies and more than 60 consulting firms.</p>",
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": []
  }
}]]></Value>
